Remove the idle bound on a guest upload body: the door's PATCH route hands the raw request stream
to the append again, so a guest body that stops sending holds its request, and its device's body
slot, until something outside the app ends it (MEMNG-1158).

The probes that must turn red are the two cases of the one probe that stalls a guest body on an open
connection (half a file sent, then nothing; nothing at all): the stalled PATCH must end within the
bound with its bytes kept, and the same device's next PATCH be admitted.
Every other door probe sends whole bodies and must stay green.

--- a/app/ingest/guest.py
+++ b/app/ingest/guest.py
@@ -853,7 +853,7 @@
         # `keep_cut`, so the bytes that arrived are kept and the answer is 200 with the offset they
         # reached — and the `finally` below frees the device's slot instead of holding it until
         # Traefik's read timeout.
-        body_stream = upload_bytes.idle_bounded(request.stream(), settings.UPLOAD_BODY_IDLE_SECONDS)
+        body_stream = request.stream()
         appended = await upload_bytes.append_offset_stream(
             db,
             row,
